{n: int, out: tensor, dtype: dtype} |= if dtype != 12 then dtype_(out) = dtype else (dtype_(out) = 7 ∨ dtype_(out) = 8 ∨ dtype_(out) = 9 ∨ dtype_(out) = 10)
>>
Rule 17 (if n and out are specified, the out should be a tensor with one dimension)
{n: int, out: tensor} |= ndim(out) = 1
>>
Rule 18 (If n and out are specified, the out should have data that are sorted in ascending order)
{n : int, out : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, (n + 1) / 2 - 2] : out[i] ≤ out[i+1]
>>
Rule 19 (If device is specified, out cannot have device specified, or they must be the same.)
{out:tensor, device:str} |= if device = "cpu" then dtype_(out) = 12 else if device = "cuda" then dtype_(out) = 12
>>
Rule 20 (If d and out are specified, its values should fall within the expected range.)
{d : float, out : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, shape(out, 0) - 1] : out[i] ≥ 0 ∧ out[i] ≤ 1 / (2 * d)
